&SAVE
Command: SAVE		Abbr: SA	Utility: none, internal to system

}SAVE dev:file.ex fnnnn-fmmmm,...;fssss=cccc

fnnnn-fmmmm	Save a contigous protion of memory from fnnnn to fmmmm.

fssss		Set the starting address where
		f = the starting field
		ssss = the starting memory address

cccc		A 4 digit number specifing the job status word where:

bit 0 = 1  File does not load into locations 00000-01777
bit 1 = 1  File does not load into locations 10000-11777
bit 2 = 1  Program must be reloaded before restarted
bit 3 = 1  Program will not destroy BATCH
bit 4 = 1  Memory image file generated by linker
bit 5      Reserved for OS278 s  set baud rate of DECmate printer port
	COL n	  Set number of columns used by DIRECT 
	ECHO	  Restore terminal character echoing
	ESC	  Echo ESC as a dollar sign
	HEIGHT n  Set number of lines sent between PAUSE
	PAGE	  enable the PAUSE function
	PAUSE n	  Set pause between "pages" from 1-85 seconds.
	SCOPE	  Erase character on terminal in response to DEL
	WIDTH n	  Set width of terminal to n (multiple of 8)

Line printer parameters:

	WIDTH n   Set width of lineprinter to n

Device handler parameters:

}SET HANDLER old new	old     = Handler to be replaced 
			new     = Handler to be inserted

Example:   }SET HANDLER RX2B R0AB     Replaces RX02 drive pair B handler
				      with RL02 handler devices A and B.

NOTE: both old and new handlers must reside on SYS: as handler.HN

}SET HANDLER /L			Display list of current handlers	

System parameters:

}SET SYS INIT file	Request execution of "file" when starting system.

Examples:

          }SET SYS INIT R LOG     will execute the file LOG.SV upon boot
	  }SET SYS INIT HELP	  will execute the CCL command HELP
	  }SET SYS INIT @NEW	  will execute the file NEW.CM

}SET SYS DEVICE logdev handler.hn

			Transfer current OS278 system to another logical
			device "logdev:". System handler to use is
			"handler.hn". Read the SET command chapter before
			doing this!


